# ContextStream (when MCP is enabled)

When the ContextStream MCP server is available:

- **Session bootstrap (mandatory—no exceptions):** On the **first message** of every new conversation, your **very first action** must be: (1) `session_init(folder_path=<repo root>, context_hint=<user's message or "WinPodiums Phase 1 MVP">)` then (2) `context_smart(user_message=<user's message>)`. Do not call any other tool or send a reply before both are done. On **every subsequent message** in that conversation, call `context_smart(user_message=<current message>)` at the start of your turn—do not skip. If ContextStream MCP is unavailable or returns no useful context, fall back to reading [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [docs/architecture/next-steps.md](../../docs/architecture/next-steps.md).
- **Code/search:** Before Grep/Read for code or docs, use ContextStream `search` (mode=hybrid or semantic) first; fall back to local tools only if needed.
- **Decisions:** Recall with session/memory tools for "why did we…"; after significant decisions, capture with title, content, and file/module path. See [development guide](../../docs/guides/development.md#ai-tooling-optional).
- **Graph:** Before refactors, use **graph(action="dependencies", ...)** and **graph(action="impact", target="...")**. After clone or first use, run **project(action="ingest_local")** once if the repo is not yet indexed; repeat after major changes. Optionally **graph(action="ingest")** for full graph (Elite/Team). Include file/module path when capturing decisions.
- **New workspace / empty memory:** If this is a new workspace or memory seems empty, run the one-time bootstrap (session_init + capture key decisions from ADRs/AGENTS.md) as in the [development guide](../../docs/guides/development.md#optional-one-time-bootstrap).
- **Lessons:** When the user corrects a mistake or says "don’t do X again", use **session(action="capture_lesson", ...)** with trigger, impact, prevention, keywords.
- **Tagging:** Repo docs use stable IDs (PRD-XXX, ADR-XXX, TP-XXX) and **Related** / **Implements**. See [ContextStream mapping](../../docs/guides/contextstream-mapping.md).
- **API docs:** Each Worker endpoint is documented in **docs/api/openapi.yaml** and served in Swagger at **/api-docs**. Smoke test ensures API documentation loads. When adding or changing API routes, update the OpenAPI spec and keep endpoints in sync.
- **Before pushing to remote:** Run local tests; **at least 80% of tests must pass** before pushing. See [Run tests before push](../../docs/guides/development.md#run-tests-before-push). Block or warn on push if the threshold is not met.

Do not duplicate [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) stack or phase here; ContextStream complements it with persistent memory and code intelligence.
